# starter.rule -- compact, high-value ruleset for:  ./crack.py --rules-file rules/starter.rule
#
# Hashcat-compatible function syntax. One rule per line; functions are applied
# left-to-right to each dictionary word to produce one candidate. Full-line '#'
# comments and blank lines are ignored (hashcat treats '#' as a literal, so an
# inline comment would be taken as text -- keep comments on their own line).
#
# When --rules-file is given it REPLACES the module's built-in mangling.

# --- identity / case ---
:
l
u
c
C
t

# --- append a single common digit ---
$1
$2
$0
$7
$9
$3

# --- append digit runs ---
$1 $2 $3
$1 $2 $3 $4
$0 $0
$1 $1
$6 $9
c $1
c $1 $2 $3

# --- append recent years ---
$1 $9 $9 $0
$2 $0 $0 $0
$2 $0 $1 $9
$2 $0 $2 $0
$2 $0 $2 $1
$2 $0 $2 $2
$2 $0 $2 $3
$2 $0 $2 $4
$2 $0 $2 $5
c $2 $0 $2 $4
c $2 $0 $2 $5

# --- append punctuation / bang ---
$!
$! $!
$.
$@
$#
$*
$1 $!
c $!
c $1 $!
c $2 $0 $2 $4 $!

# --- prepend ---
^1
^!
^1 ^2 ^3
^0 ^0

# --- reverse / duplicate / reflect ---
r
d
f
c f
c r

# --- leet substitutions ---
sa@
se3
si1
so0
ss$
sa4
si!
sa@ se3
so0 si1
sa@ se3 si1 so0
sa@ se3 si1 so0 ss$
c sa@ se3
c sa@ $1
c se3 $1 $2 $3
c so0 $2 $0 $2 $4
ss$ $1 $2 $3

# --- toggle / edge-char tricks ---
T0
c T0
z1
Z1
$s
c $s
] $1
[ $1
